    "28": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Standards check",
          "heading": "Farrell says Ireland are raising the standard before Fiji, after 30-point win",
          "body": "Friday night's win over Argentina moved Ireland top of the northern hemisphere table for at least 24 hours, and Ireland head coach Farrell said the aim is to keep improving in every area and to show the squad what is acceptable. \"I suppose it's raising the standard to be as good as we possibly can,\" he said. The response followed a 40-21 defeat by the All Blacks at Eden Park. Fiji are next, in Round 5 of the Nations Championship."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 with Beauden Barrett scoring twice",
          "body": "Wales beat Japan ahead of All Blacks Test. France lose Romain Ntamack for rest of Nations Championship."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "RTÉ Sport Rugby"
      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team news",
          "heading": "Furbank returns at full-back as Fin Smith passes fitness test for Australia",
          "body": "England's Fin Smith has been declared fit after a scare in the build-up, and George Furbank returns at full-back for the first time since November 2024, when injuries and a bout of appendicitis in the July window kept him out of the Test side. Smith has started each of England's past five outings at fly-half, usurping George Ford in the process. Greg Fisilau is in the match-day squad and could win his maiden Test cap off the bench."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 with Beauden Barrett scoring twice",
          "body": "Wales beat Japan ahead of All Blacks Test. France lose Romain Ntamack for rest of Nations Championship."
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Allianz Stadium, Twickenham, London"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Planet Rugby"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "France lose Romain Ntamack for rest of Nations Championship after shoulder injury",
          "body": "Head coach Fabien Galthié confirmed to TF1 that Romain Ntamack will miss the rest of the Nations Championship after injuring his left shoulder during Saturday's 54-17 win over Fiji in Lyon. \"Romain went off with this injury and we won't have him for the rest of the competition,\" Galthié said. Ntamack was forced off after just 34 minutes, and no recovery timetable has been announced pending further assessment. Matthieu Jalibert is also unavailable, so France must find a replacement at ten ahead of the South Africa test."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 with Beauden Barrett scoring twice",
          "body": "Wales beat Japan ahead of All Blacks Test."
        }
      ]
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching verdict",
          "heading": "Andy Farrell wants Ireland 'more ruthless' despite six-try Argentina win",
          "body": "Ireland coach Andy Farrell said there is still room for improvement after the 42-12 win over Argentina, despite six tries to two. \"How we can be a little bit more ruthless because that's the team that we want to be,\" he said. Lock Tadhg Beirne agreed that some of the tries were proper team efforts but felt the side could have scored more. Fiji come next, before the world champion Springboks."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 with Beauden Barrett scoring twice",
          "body": "Wales beat Japan ahead of All Blacks Test. France lose Romain Ntamack for rest of Nations Championship."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "SA Rugby Magazine"
      }
    },
    "389": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coach's review",
          "heading": "Quesada credits Italy's forwards and maul defence after 66-7 Springboks loss",
          "body": "Italy head coach Gonzalo Quesada, speaking after the defeat in Turin, said his forwards had produced a performance of notable quality, pointing to closing out of phases and maul defence against a side hard to stop on the five-metre line. He said the kicking game and restarts did not work. Quesada added that Italy at times put themselves under pressure, but in the second half, up to the 70th minute, they had more ball and possession and scored a try."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 with Beauden Barrett scoring twice",
          "body": "Wales beat Japan ahead of All Blacks Test. France lose Romain Ntamack for rest of Nations Championship."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Federazione Italiana Rugby"
      }
    },
    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Discipline reckoning",
          "heading": "Sione Tuipulotu takes 'full responsibility' for sin-binning in All Blacks defeat",
          "body": "Captain Sione Tuipulotu said Scotland's discipline \"wasn't good enough, and it starts with me\" after the 43-21 defeat at Murrayfield. Moments after he was sin-binned on 50 minutes, Beauden Barrett scored his second try, with Scotland conceding 13 penalties to New Zealand's eight. Tuipulotu said they were \"nowhere near accurate enough\" in the second half, and described next week's Australia match as a must-win game."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales beat Japan ahead of All Blacks Test",
          "body": "France lose Romain Ntamack for rest of Nations Championship."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection debate",
          "heading": "Warburton and Biggar urge Tandy against wholesale changes for All Blacks test",
          "body": "Sam Warburton and Dan Biggar, speaking on ITV after the Japan win, want head coach Steve Tandy to keep changes limited for the All Blacks. Warburton said he favours Warren Gatland's approach, arguing that just because a performance has been \"slightly underwhelming doesn't mean you make wholesale changes.\" He also suggested front-row changes could be considered, pointing to Rhys Carre, Ryan Elias and Tomas Francis, who came on after half-time and helped Wales gain ascendancy at scrum time. Carre, in particular, made a strong impact."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 with Beauden Barrett scoring twice",
          "body": "France lose Romain Ntamack for rest of Nations Championship."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "WalesOnline"
      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Discipline issue",
          "heading": "Efraín Elías yellow-carded as Pumas' forwards are disrupted in Dublin",
          "body": "Efraín Elías was yellow-carded for a high tackle on Hugo Keenan, and Ireland's final try, a Rónan Kelleher lineout maul, came against a seven-man Pumas pack. Justo Piccardo had earlier been yellow-carded for offside, and Ireland led 21-5 at half-time. Ireland won the Aviva Stadium contest 42-12 on Friday, with Keenan's hat-trick completed on 49 minutes."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 with Beauden Barrett scoring twice",
          "body": "Wales beat Japan ahead of All Blacks Test. France lose Romain Ntamack for rest of Nations Championship."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Americas Rugby News"
      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-08",
      "edition": "Sunday 8 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captain's message",
          "heading": "Harry Wilson urges Wallabies to 'play our own game' against England",
          "body": "Ahead of the opener, Wilson said the Wallabies \"definitely want to be us\", pointing to the 42-38 win over South Africa in Perth in September, when they backed their skills and kept attacking. The captain said the two New Zealand defeats, where Australia conceded 93 points, had taught lessons that must be carried forward. Coach Les Kiss has warned that England's back three can do damage if given space, and does not expect a forward battle alone. England have lost five of their last seven Tests."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand beat Scotland 43-21 with Beauden Barrett scoring twice",
          "body": "Wales beat Japan ahead of All Blacks Test. France lose Romain Ntamack for rest of Nations Championship."
        }
      ],
